WEBVTT

NOTE Hidden reference scan: jtressle, CC BY 4.0. https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/san-francisco-painted-ladies-cf5aeb7fb0ac4152b43f72ce1dac60d6

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.002
This is Cortex. This recording uses synthetic vocal profiles to drive a real MuJoCo simulation. The robot is simulated, and the Painted Ladies are modeled architecture in a three dimensional park scene. This is an architectural study, not a photoreal digital twin.

00:00:11.002 --> 00:00:18.283
The camera moves around modeled Painted Ladies. The buildings have side walls, roofs, projecting windows, stairs and geometric depth. A modeled Alamo Square path gives the robot a bounded walking area.

00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:27.236
Keyboard and voice share the same tools. Hold a direction: the robot turns first, then walks. Release to pause. Named targets pass through planning and the reflex gate.

00:00:27.236 --> 00:00:37.054
First, the calm profile. Come here. The robot approaches at a moderate pace, with a comfortable stopping distance.

00:00:37.054 --> 00:00:47.218
Reset. Exactly the same words, with a higher-intensity acoustic profile. Priority rises and the walking policy changes. The feet are driven by Unitree’s frozen locomotion controller.

00:00:47.218 --> 00:00:57.979
Reveal Cortex. Measured acoustic cues become a documented behavioral policy. Speed, approach distance and confirmation are explicit. The live microphone path is implemented through Gradium and Pipecat.

00:00:57.979 --> 00:01:05.260
A hesitant acoustic profile does not simply make the robot faster. It holds for confirmation, reduces approach speed, and gives the person more space.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:14.891
Now memory. Save the scene, then ask where the backpack was seen. Cortex retrieves the actual captured frame and its registered location, beside the planter.

00:01:14.891 --> 00:01:20.894
Take me there. The retrieved sighting becomes a waypoint, and the robot turns toward the planter.

00:01:20.894 --> 00:01:30.666
Wait. Stop. The reflex bypasses the planner, latches the stop, and measures acknowledgement and physical settling separately.

00:01:30.666 --> 00:01:39.180
Continue, but slowly. A deliberate resume releases the stop and applies a lower speed ceiling. Vocal delivery can change behavior. It can never turn safety off.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:49.717
Cortex gives physical AI perception, memory, reasoning, reflexes, and safe action. Gradium handles voice, Pipecat carries the conversation, and SambaNova plans the next safe action.
